The user's question: "right now does the mod show the icon of the server waypoint on the voxel map?" Answer: yes, it shows VoxelMap's built-in icon images, chosen from a fixed suffix list — so the server waypoint's *item* icon (from game items) is not shown; instead a mapped VoxelMap image is used.

Then: "if not can you make it shows the icon from the game items to show on voxel map as well, idk if we should modify server waypoint source code or voxel map source code".

Let me check WaypointIconPolicy.voxelMapSuffixes and how server waypoint icons work (does the server use item icons?).

Also check the VoxelMap code for how waypoint icons are rendered — VoxelMap waypoint icons come from its own texture `waypoint.png` / `icons.png` sheets, and imageSuffix selects a sub-image. To render arbitrary game item icons, VoxelMap's `Waypoint` class would have to support rendering a custom icon, e.g., an ItemStack. That's a change to VoxelMap source (which the user has locally, since the mod's build uses `voxelmap_<loader>` property pinning a VoxelMap-Updated build — likely a local maven build).

